SUMMARY = """Russia and Ukraine agreed to a large-scale prisoner exchange on the final day of US-mediated peace talks in Abu Dhabi, the first such talks in nine months. Neither side disclosed numbers. US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner were set to meet Presidents Putin and Zelensky separately the next day. Ukrainian officials called the discussions constructive.

The Iran war continued. Israel struck the Nasser Medical Complex in Khan Younis, killing six people including a surgeon and wounding over twenty. Iran attacked ship navigation systems on Didamar Island in Oman. Iranian officials said the Strait of Hormuz would never return to its pre-war status and displayed underground missile stocks while lifting their self-imposed range limit.

In the United States, House Republicans blocked impeachment charges against Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth by a 211–204 procedural vote. Jim Jordan was elected the next House Minority Leader. Democrat Scott Colom was projected to win the Mississippi Senate race, becoming the state’s first Black senator since Reconstruction.

Elsewhere, the historic ocean liner SS United States was deliberately sunk off Florida to create the world’s largest artificial reef. Confirmed Ebola cases in the Democratic Republic of the Congo surpassed 11,000 with more than 5,300 deaths. Portugal closed thousands of schools as Storm Charles approached."""

